# File: scripts/__tests__/
# Generated from: specs/560-close-the-gaps-left-open-after-556-lock-pid-reuse-reclaim-guard-put-back-spec-revision-publishing-and-untested-paths/requirements.md
Feature: Close the gaps left open after #556

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A lock whose holder pid was reused is broken
    Given a lock whose holder record names a live pid with a different start token
    When another process waits on the lock
    Then the lock is broken at once
    And a holder with a matching or unreadable start token is not broken

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A reclaim guard is never put back over another process's guard
    Given a process that moved a fresh guard while breaking a stale one
    When another process has taken the guard path meanwhile
    Then the moved guard is not restored over it and the taken guard stays

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A revised spec publishes after an earlier spec PR merged
    Given a spec branch with a merged spec PR at another head and a changed spec package
    When the publish helper merges the spec
    Then it opens a new spec-only PR and merges it at its exact head
    And an unchanged package reports the latest merged PR without a new PR

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A remote default branch with no specs directory reads as absent
    Given a readable remote ref without a specs directory
    When the spec status is read from it
    Then no spec_status_unreadable reason is reported

  @SCN005
  Scenario: The #556 paths have regression tests
    Given the changelog-merge and remote spec-check paths
    When the tests run
    Then a failed git show aborts to conflict, a failed fetch fails approved_spec_missing, a later-merged spec is found, and a kept bullet is rolled into the version section
    And a bullet present with a star marker is not added again
